    "summary": "Implemented a fixed opt-in slow-vm timing policy across coordinator, manager, worker, Git, runtime I/O, resource drains and CI/operator containment while preserving normal numeric defaults, exact integrity, wire formats and ownership proof. Repeated drains share a cumulative ceiling and independently reobserve closure. Tasks1–6 are accepted, including actual fresh UTM Node22.22.1/npm10.9.4 live acquisition, zero-network reuse and native-consumer qualification with independent parent/worker closure. Final current-source scoped regression passed306 tests across67 files:284 tests in62 canonical files plus22 tests in5 direct serial controller files, with zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo. Independent audit verifies exact coverage, all16 LLD subjects, unchanged source/output fingerprints and all71 canonical plus48 controller command-group closures. The first normal-cap attempt remains failed/incomplete with verified cleanup; the full rerun used declared40-minute file/4-hour run bounds and repeated all62 canonical files. Approved separate ISSUE-e1aed06b860a76cb reconciled two stale controller test files; production inputs are otherwise identical to the UTM source. Evidence committed in eb47d3528; test source b06fb951d955e707408c246011a4c61aa1bd6ee0 remains byte-identical. Earlier isolated stale controller attempt remains blocked and untouched outside current main-checkout runs. No host daemon/Ollama update or activation, release enablement, current Linux/Windows qualification or foundation/S4 completion is claimed.",
